    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup leans heavily into aggressive base-running and high-ceiling individual matchups. **Corbin Carroll** leads the pack with an elite 79.77 efficiency score; he is a locked-in start, particularly because the slow delivery of Quantrill facilitates his stolen base upside. Similarly, **James Wood** (76.56) and **Mickey Moniak** (74.02) represent our most potent levers, with **James Wood** benefiting from an elite .415 xwOBA and a prime lead-off spot against a favorable 4.61 xERA matchup, while **Mickey Moniak** thrives on a massive 14% platoon edge against Jobe. **Josh Naylor** also warrants attention; despite the handedness disadvantage, his 72.22 score is propelled by a 19% boost from a soft matchup against Lopez.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Griffin Conine** on the bench. While his 43.39 score suggested utility potential, he was squeezed out by the sheer efficiency of our lower-order starters who possess better park factors and situational platoon advantages. We are monitoring the defensive metrics of the opposition closely, as **Austin Riley** carries a slight negative risk against an elite 1.86s catcher pop-time, though his 59.36 score remains safely within our \"Strong\" tier. While **Max Muncy** carries a sub-60 score, his elite 36-PA BvP history and the potential to exploit the pitcher\u2019s 88% SB allowance make him a high-leverage pivot in the middle infield. We are keeping a close watch on weather reports, though no immediate risks currently threaten the slate; we continue to proceed with caution on **Tyler Soderstrom** as he remains sidelined on the IL.",
